  "issues": [
    "mixed-two-part-different-finishes: candidate accepts an incomplete/semantically wrong per-part finish plan",
    "solid-unknown-look-token: lookRequest suppresses clarification while permissive offlinePart produces a black roof plan",
    "solid-ambiguous-part-scope: lookRequest suppresses clarification while offlinePart expands “roof or hood” into both parts"
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "finding": "Mixed per-part instructions are represented as a complete but wrong plan: the red “solid” roof is assigned matte because offlinePartCoverage applies the request-wide matte finish from the separate hood clause."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "finding": "For malformed/ambiguous solid-color requests, the changed lookRequest returns null even though offlinePartCoverage rejects; the downstream offlinePart classifier still emits a partial or guessed action (black roof for “Black Ice Nebula”; both hood and roof for “roof or hood”). Frozen baseline lookRequest returned a look query for these examples, intercepting the fallback path."
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This review loads the exact real SpbProDesign module API in a VM and invokes actual lookRequest/offlineSpec/offlinePart/offlineElement/offlinePartCoverage/compoundPlan classifiers. It does not load public SpbProAI dispatcher or owner/source proof, and does not claim an applied route. The observed fallback hazard is classifier-level and must be replayed in the eventual controller before integration acceptance. No providers, native app, browser, or paint application."
  ]
